      "exact_frozen_census_obligation": "W01 represents Spin(4) by independent left/right SU(2)=Sp(1) actions, with the Euclidean vector action x -> g_L x g_R^{-1}; the two factors are structurally independent in Euclidean signature. W01 §2.1 explicitly prints x maps to g_L*x*g_R^(-1) for Euclidean SU(2) left/right factors and says (g_L,g_R) and (-g_L,-g_R) determine the same SO(4) rotation, giving the source Spin(4) double-cover claim. The sign-paired representatives are not identical Spin-group elements. In the quaternion presentation SU(2)=Sp(1) is the unit-quaternion group with independent left and right multiplication and the imaginary-time coordinate maps to the identity. W01 §2.1 also singles out DIMENSION FOUR as an exceptional rotation-group factorization: in the author's words, rotations are not a simple group there but have the stated two-factor structure. This is conserved as Woit's dimension-scoped explanatory assertion, not an independently established classification theorem or a literal identity of SO(4) with SU(2)_L×SU(2)_R.",
