      "exact_frozen_census_obligation": "W01 identifies the common complexification of Euclidean, Minkowski, and split-signature four-vector spaces with M(2,C)=Hom(S_R,S_L), while retaining different real-form/action constraints for each signature. W01 separately prints the Minkowski embedding x=-i(x0*1+x1*sigma1+x2*sigma2+x3*sigma3) with determinant -x0^2+x1^2+x2^2+x3^2; the split E(2,2) model consists of REAL 2x2 matrices [[x0+x3,x1+x2],[x1-x2,x0-x3]] with determinant x0^2-x1^2+x2^2-x3^2. All three real spaces complexify to M(2,C), but they do not carry the same real-form constraint. The printed Minkowski Lorentz action is x maps to inverse(adjoint(g)) * x * inverse(g) for g in SL(2,C); the split-signature Spin(2,2)=SL(2,R)_L x SL(2,R)_R action is x maps to g_L*x*inverse(g_R). These typed group actions differ from the Euclidean Spin(4) real-form action, even though complexification is shared. W01 §2.2 separately states spinor carriers S_R,S_L with complexified vectors Hom(S_R,S_L), using R2 in split E(2,2) but C2 for E4 and E3,1. In Euclidean E4 the two spinor spaces transform independently, whereas Minkowski SL(2,C) action g on S_R forces the (g^dagger)^(-1) action on S_L. A twistor spacetime point is a C2 plane S_R inside T=C4, with its point-relative quotient S_L=T/S_R and tangent Hom(S_R,S_L). The complex Grassmannian G_2,4(C) carries the SL(4,C) conformal action with source-ordered real subgroup/compactification correspondences Spin(5,1)/E4/S4, Spin(4,2)/E3,1/(S3×S1), Spin(3,3)/E2,2/G_2,4(R); do not equate the real forms or promote source claims to new proofs.",
